DESCRIPTION:The A.I.R. Fellowship Program for Emerging and Underrepresented
  Women and Non-Binary Artists\, established in 1993 by artist Stephanie Be
 rnheim\, annually awards six emerging artists based in New York City their
  first solo exhibition in NYC with the support of the A.I.R. community\; m
 ore than 130 artists have come through the program. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 3\
 ,000 stipend\, a solo exhibition at A.I.R. Gallery in spring/summer 2028\,
  4 to 5 professional development workshops\, an assigned artist-mentor\, a
  one-on-one studio visit with a review panelist\, and curatorial and staff
  support across the 12-month fellowship (September 2027 to August 2028). W
 HO IS ELIGIBLE: women and non-binary visual artists working in any media\,
  18 or older\, resident in the five boroughs of New York City for the full
  fellowship\; you must not have had a solo exhibition at a permanent NYC v
 enue in the last 10 years\, must not be enrolled in a degree-granting prog
 ram during the fellowship\, must not be in a comparable development progra
 m\, and must not be an A.I.R. staff/board member or fellowship alum. SELEC
 TION PANEL for this cycle: Ada Potter\, Jo-ey Tang and Mindy Seu. DEADLINE
 : 10 November 2026\, 11:59pm ET. TO APPLY: via Submittable\, linked from t
 he program page.\n\nOrganisation: A.I.R. Gallery\nLocation: New York City.
  Applicants must be residents of the five boroughs for the full fellowship
  duration.\nAward: USD 3\,000 stipend per fellow\, plus a solo exhibition 
 at A.I.R. Gallery\, 4 to 5 professional development workshops\, an assigne
 d artist-mentor\, a studio visit with a review panelist and ongoing staff 
 support. Six fellows selected. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 12-mo
 nth fellowship\, September 2027 to August 2028\; solo exhibition in spring
 /summer 2028\n\nMore: https://www.airgallery.org/fellowship-program-2027-2
 028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
