SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Push: Black Utopian Fellowship 2027 (New York Cit
 y)
DESCRIPTION:The Black Utopian Fellowship is a yearlong incubator fellowship
  created by #DayOnesArt in collaboration with Culture Push\, for Black art
 ists\, researchers\, scientists and inventors\, with career development an
 d mentorship through Black-run institutions. The 2027 call\, themed Return
  to Real\, asks for project proposals that critique what is real in 2026 a
 round themes such as economics\, health\, artificial intelligence\, cultur
 e\, politics\, media and the education system\, and that explore how legac
 y is taught\, inherited and reimagined across generations. The Fellowship 
 for Utopian Practice is the umbrella program and the same guidelines apply
 : a USD 2\,250 stipend\, fiscal sponsorship\, mentoring\, and access to Ma
 terials for the Arts. ELIGIBILITY: Black artists and other professionals i
 n any discipline with at least 3 years of experience\; currently enrolled 
 undergraduates cannot apply\; group proposals welcome\; projects must be n
 ew\, socially engaged\, without prior institutional support\, and grounded
  in a specific NYC neighborhood or community\; fellows must live within co
 mmuting distance of New York City. Applicants may apply to only one Cultur
 e Push fellowship per cycle\; unselected themed applications pass into the
  General Fellowship pool. CONTACT: buf@culturepush.org. DEADLINE: 15 Octob
 er 2026 at 11:59 pm ET.\n\nOrganisation: Culture Push\nLocation: New York 
 City\, US. Project work must occur within the five boroughs and fellows mu
 st live within commuting distance of NYC.\nAward: USD 2\,250 stipend\, plu
 s fiscal sponsorship for fundraising\, mentorship and strategizing support
 \, per the umbrella Fellowship for Utopian Practice guidelines. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: One calendar year\, January to December 2027.\n\nMore
 : https://www.culturepush.org/2027-black-utopian-fellowship?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.culturepush.org/2027-black-utopian-fellowship?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, US. Project work must occur within the five boroug
 hs and fellows must live within commuting distance of NYC.
END:VEVENT
