 (New York City)
DESCRIPTION:Culture Push's yearlong Disability Arts + Dreaming Fellowship s
 upports self-identifying disabled artists\, organizers\, creative thinkers
  and collectives developing disability-centered\, seed-stage projects that
  treat Access as Art or collective accessibility and advance emergent Disa
 bility Culture and Justice within the five boroughs of NYC. It centers Dis
 ability Justice as a way of moving together across disability\, race\, sex
 uality\, gender and class\, with mixed-abilities programming\, access chec
 k-ins\, co-thinking and strategizing meetings across the fellowship year. 
 The Fellowship for Utopian Practice is the umbrella program and the same g
 uidelines apply: a USD 2\,250 stipend\, fiscal sponsorship\, a Thought Par
 tner and mentors in the field. ELIGIBILITY: at least 3 years of experience
 \; currently enrolled undergraduates cannot apply\; group proposals welcom
 e\; projects must be new\, socially engaged\, without prior institutional 
 support\, and grounded in a specific NYC neighborhood or community\; fello
 ws must live within commuting distance of New York City. Applicants may ap
 ply to only one Culture Push fellowship per cycle\; unselected themed appl
 ications pass into the General Fellowship pool. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026 
 at 11:59 pm ET.\n\nOrganisation: Culture Push\nLocation: New York City\, U
 S. Project work must occur within the five boroughs and fellows must live 
 within commuting distance of NYC.\nAward: USD 2\,250 stipend\, plus fiscal
  sponsorship for fundraising\, a Thought Partner\, mentors in the field\, 
 and access check-ins\, per the umbrella Fellowship for Utopian Practice gu
 idelines. No application fee.\nDuration: One calendar year\, January 2027 
 to January 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.culturepush.org/2027-disability-arts
 -fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
